    <div class="container">
        <h1>Welcome to Your Express Data API Server!</h1>
        <p>This is a simple static HTML page being served directly by your Express.js backend. It demonstrates how to serve static assets alongside your API.</p>
        <p>Your server is running on port <code>3000</code>.</p>

        <h2>API Endpoints:</h2>
        <p>You can interact with these endpoints using tools like Postman, Insomnia, or the <code>curl</code> command-line tool.</p>
        <ul>
            <li><code>GET /api/items</code> - Retrieve a list of all items.</li>
            <li><code>GET /api/items/:id</code> - Retrieve a single item by its ID. (e.g., <a href="/api/items/1">/api/items/1</a>)</li>
            <li><code>POST /api/items</code> - Add a new item. Requires a JSON body like: <code>{ "name": "New Task", "description": "Details about the new task." }</code></li>
            <li><code>PUT /api/items/:id</code> - Update an existing item by its ID. Requires a JSON body like: <code>{ "name": "Updated Task", "description": "New details for the task." }</code></li>
            <li><code>DELETE /api/items/:id</code> - Delete an item by its ID.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Example Usage (using <code>curl</code> in your terminal):</h2>
        <pre>
# Get all items
curl http://localhost:3000/api/items

# Get item with ID 1
curl http://localhost:3000/api/items/1

# Add a new item
curl -X POST \
     -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
     -d '{"name":"New Project Idea","description":"Develop a full-stack application."}' \
     http://localhost:3000/api/items

# Update item with ID 1
curl -X PUT \
     -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
     -d '{"name":"Updated Item A","description":"This item has been revised."}' \
     http://localhost:3000/api/items/1

# Delete item with ID 2
curl -X DELETE http://localhost:3000/api/items/2
        </pre>

        <p>Explore the <code>server.js</code> file to understand how these endpoints are implemented.</p>
        <p>Happy coding!</p>
    </div>
</body>
